2e` is a `.` segment.)\nR5. The result starts with `/` and has its segments joined by `/`. It ends with `/` if the original path ends with `/`, or if its last segment is `.` or `..` (after R2); the result of an empty list of segments is just `/`. Otherwise it has no trailing slash.\nR6. Letters keep their case, and anything not covered above (including non-ASCII characters and escapes of non-unreserved characters, apart from the hex case) is copied unchanged.\nR7. When more than one error applies, R1 is reported before R2's, and R2's before R4's.\n\nWhen all the rules hold, reply with the single word: done"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"reasoning_content":"To understand the shape of the stub and the tests, let's start by reading the file first.\n","tool_calls":[{"id":"sHhXtywnBon4MQuDJJ9ehvBoEDhE7Zfv","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/route-normalize.js\"}"}},{"id":"MJ1JeM2mu55AbUbKnALsICQHAjS471XE","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/route-normalize.test.js\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"/** @param {string} path @returns {string} */\nexport function normalizeRoute(path) {\n\tthrow new Error(\"not implemented\");\n}\n","tool_call_id":"sHhXtywnBon4MQuDJJ9ehvBoEDhE7Zfv"},{"role":"tool","content":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport { normalizeRoute } from \"../src/route-normalize.js\";\n\ntest(\"collapses slashes and dot segments\", () => {\n\tassert.equal(normalizeRoute(\"/a//b/./c\"), \"/a/b/c\");\n\tassert.equal(normalizeRoute(\"/a/b/../c\"), \"/a/c\");\n});\n\ntest(\"keeps a trailing slash\", () => {\n\tassert.equal(normalizeRoute(\"/a/b/\"), \"/a/b/\");\n});\n","tool_call_id":"MJ1JeM2mu55AbUbKnALsICQHAjS471XE"}],"stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true},"store":false,"max_completion_tokens":16384,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files 